<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blaise Diagne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1872–1934</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Blaise Diagne was a Senegalese politician, elected in 1914 as deputy for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/four-communes">Four Communes of Senegal</a>, the first black African in the French Chamber of Deputies. His laws of 1915 and 1916 confirmed the French citizenship of the communes' inhabitants. In 1918 he recruited tens of thousands of West African soldiers for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, and he later served as under-secretary of state for the colonies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blaise-diagne.jpg" alt="Blaise Diagne" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agence Meurisse (domaine public, voir fiche détaillée Gallica) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blaise_Diagne-1921.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
